75 #edb/ref 17592186442310 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442320 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442320 1077 "field-1" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442320 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442310 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442320 1079 #uuid "60abe397-ada8-52f7-89c3-1ccbe2f29023" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442303 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442305 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442309 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442311 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442313 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1077 "selection" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442309 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442321 1079 #uuid "d0e871fb-e944-567c-b4fe-9835a0a9327f" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442322 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442318 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442322 1069 "q-89745" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442322 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442322 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 2).$" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442322 1072 #uuid "365bf094-f659-5822-bf63-2e5a6992d995" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442322 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is $F(2)=1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{6}}=\\frac{63}{64}.$" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442323 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442320 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442323 1069 "q-210763" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442323 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442323 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-|5x|},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2},\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442323 1072 #uuid "7e1280de-34a4-5310-b0ea-3ca5ec3ba975" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442323 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-5t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{5t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-5t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-5t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-5t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442324 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442319 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442324 1069 "q-210785" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442324 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442324 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{8}{9},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442324 1072 #uuid "990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442324 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}(-\\frac{2}{9}t+\\frac{8}{9})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(-\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}x-\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}({x}^{2}-8x+7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7), & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442325 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442321 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442325 1069 "q-89621" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442325 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442325 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{64}x(16-{x}^{2}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442325 1072 #uuid "e65ef0d7-6649-5f56-9e79-7407f7595f66" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442325 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability density function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0<x<4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{64}t(16-{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{64}(8{t}^{2}-\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4})|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442326 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442330 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442326 1062 #uuid "24fe79a9-1c18-5367-b5d5-50f26230d23d" 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442326 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442322 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442327 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442326 13194139534880 17592186045417 true] [17592186442327 1062 #uuid "443